config OP6893_CCCI_LK_INSPECT
	tristate "Inspect op6893 LK modem handoff without starting the modem"
	depends on ARCH_MEDIATEK && OF && HAS_IOMEM
	help
	  Validate a bounded snapshot of LK's modem tags and the AP shared-memory
	  layout. This does not power, reset or communicate with the modem or SCP.
	  The board's modem-handoff node is disabled until explicitly enabled for
	  a read-only experiment. No raw tag payloads are exposed.

config OP6893_CCCI_SMEM
	bool "Validate op6893 6297 shared-memory subregions from LK"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_LK_INSPECT
	help
	  Validate the same-board noncached layout and cached aggregates, including
	  runtime data, CCISM and NVRAM cache. Preserve LK offsets and bank spans
	  instead of summing region sizes across gaps. Reject aliases, truncation
	  and unsupported IDs. No shared-memory mapping, clearing or modem start.
	  Disabled by default; extends the explicit LK handoff inspection only.

config OP6893_CCCI_MD_PLATFORM
	bool "Own op6893 cold modem platform power without releasing the MD CPU"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_LK_INSPECT=y && OP6893_CCCI_SMEM
	depends on PM_GENERIC_DOMAINS && REGULATOR && MFD_SYSCON
	depends on MTK_SCPSYS_PM_DOMAINS
	depends on COMMON_CLK_MT6893
	help
	  Retain validated LK shared-memory geometry and own the four supplies,
	  four ordinary CCIF clocks and explicitly attached MD1 domain. Expose
	  an explicit LK CHECK_DONE and inherited-domain power-off, then one cold
	  on/off cycle using this boot's unchanged enabled-rail voltage baseline.
	  Do not change voltages, release the MD CPU or access shared memory/CCIF.
	  Probe preserves LK's domain state. Disabled by default;
	  cannot coexist with the metadata-only node for the same LK buffer.

config OP6893_CCCI_CCIF
	bool "Prepare op6893 ordinary CCIF hardware and 6297 rings"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_MD_PLATFORM && OF_IRQ
	help
	  Reserve AP/MD CCIF windows, two NO_AUTOEN IRQs and the adjacent normal/
	  exception CCISM banks in the existing owner. An explicit prepare after
	  controlled MD power-on formats both sets of 16 rings, resets CCIF0 and
	  initializes/verifies SRAM and debug geometry. IRQs stay masked until
	  a future owner installs a receive consumer and explicitly starts RX.
	  Includes bounded ring helpers, IRQ/work/STOP synchronization and SRAM
	  HS1/header decoders. No start caller, MD CPU release, doorbell, runtime
	  negotiation or FS/NVRAM access is added.

config OP6893_CCCI_HANDSHAKE
	bool "Build the op6893 CCIF runtime response and control consumer"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_CCIF
	help
	  Reserve/map the runtime subregion's enclosing pages in the existing
	  owner. Add bounded 64-slot feature negotiation, the v2.1 SRAM response,
	  BUSY/doorbell publishing and a timed HS1/HS2 control consumer. No I/O at
	  probe; no sysfs start or CPU-release caller is installed. A future owner
	  must provide real capabilities, SCP/CCISM and FS/NVRAM service gates.
	  No new modem, filesystem or radio readiness is claimed by enabling this.

config OP6893_CCCI_RESOURCES
	tristate "Check op6893 modem regulator and ordinary CCIF clock references"
	depends on ARCH_MEDIATEK && OF && REGULATOR
	depends on COMMON_CLK_MT6893
	help
	  Acquire the four modem supply references and the four ordinary CCIF
	  clock references without enabling them. This only checks framework
	  dependencies; it does not access CCIF, start MD/SCP or report readiness.
	  The resource node and SID3 provider are disabled in the board DT.
	  Enabling providers also requires review of their probe and shutdown
	  behavior; a successful reference lookup is not a hardware validation.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_PROTOCOL
	bool "Build op6893 SCP RV mailbox layout and CCCI protocol helpers"
	depends on ARCH_MEDIATEK
	help
	  Build the bounded mailbox layout validator, APCCCI message codec and
	  SCP region-header decoder with recovery mapping bounds checks.
	  This is preparatory code for the SCP transport and CCISM bridge, not
	  a mailbox or remoteproc driver. It registers no device, accesses no
	  hardware and cannot start SCP/MD or report either processor ready.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_AWAKE
	bool "Build the op6893 SCP RV shared AP awake backend"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_PROTOCOL && REGMAP
	help
	  Build the bounded, sleepable AP awake handshake over a caller-supplied
	  infracfg syscon regmap. A future shared provider must establish real SCP
	  READY, serialize all consumers and coordinate clocks, STOP and reset.
	  This registers no device and has no caller or automatic hardware access.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_RESTORE_PLAN
	bool "Build the op6893 SCP non-secure recovery layout checker"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_PROTOCOL
	help
	  Check an exact CPU header snapshot against independent firmware/share
	  reservations and the same-board TCM resource. Bound the loader/header
	  targets, two-core live/backup DRAM layout and disjoint source windows.
	  This only produces geometry; it cannot prove image or backup validity,
	  reset completion, old-message isolation or READY. No device, mappings,
	  copying, reset or IRQ actions, or platform caller are added.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_RESOURCE_HOLD
	bool "Allow explicit op6893 boot-lifetime SCP 26 MHz resource pin"
	depends on ARCH_MEDIATEK && OF
	depends on COMMON_CLK_MT6893
	help
	  Add one built-in owner of the same-board ATF SCP resource request
	  channel. Explicit sysfs reads query bounded resource bookkeeping;
	  writing 26m to pin sends at most one additive 26 MHz request and
	  verifies SCP resource membership. No SMC is sent at probe. A failure
	  is sticky, with no retry, fallback ABI or release operation. A pin
	  lasts until reboot, since release would clear inherited SCP votes.
	  This does not start SCP/MD, access their registers or establish READY.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_CFG_RESERVE
	bool "Reserve op6893 SCP cfg in the boot-lifetime resource owner"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_RESOURCE_HOLD && HAS_IOMEM
	help
	  Reserve and map the complete same-board SCP cfg window in the existing
	  boot-lifetime resource owner. Reject a different address or size and
	  conflicting resource claims. The mapping performs no register reads or
	  writes and exposes no completion operation. It prepares exclusive cfg
	  ownership for a future serialized RX/IRQ/reset implementation.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_OBSERVE
	tristate "Observe op6893 AP-side SCP clock and memory prerequisites"
	depends on ARCH_MEDIATEK && OF_RESERVED_MEM && MFD_SYSCON
	help
	  Expose the inherited SCP mux selector/gate through the existing TOPCK
	  syscon and report this boot's firmware/share reservation bookkeeping.
	  The board node is disabled by default. Without the additional explicit
	  diagnostic options, no SCP MMIO, TCM, firmware,
	  mailbox, awake, clock control, reset or READY access is performed.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_BOOTSTRAP_HOLD
	bool "Hold the constrained op6893 SCP bootstrap clock during observation"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_OBSERVE=y
	depends on COMMON_CLK_MT6893
	help
	  Acquire and enable the TOPCK SCP output before exposing observations.
	  The provider accepts only the inherited 26 MHz ungated condition and
	  retains a critical reference after consumer failure or removal. This
	  does not request SPM resources, start SCP or establish READY.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_CORE0_OBSERVE
	bool "Allow explicit op6893 SCP core0 reset/status readback"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_OBSERVE && HAS_IOMEM
	help
	  Map only the same-board core0 configuration resource. An explicit
	  core0 sysfs read samples reset aliases and gated/halt bits twice,
	  gated by before/after AP mux observations. No automatic MMIO reads,
	  reset writes, TCM access, mailbox, awake or READY claim is made.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_TCM_OBSERVE
	bool "Allow explicit op6893 SCP TCM header observation"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_OBSERVE=y
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_CORE0_OBSERVE && OP6893_CCCI_SCP_PROTOCOL
	help
	  Map only the header window at TCM+4 and accept exact 68/72-byte
	  snapshots with before/after core0 and AP mux checks. Decode only
	  bounded metadata and report sizes and reservation containment.
	  No raw header, code or unknown fields are exported. This does not
	  load firmware, map recovery buffers, release reset or establish READY.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_RX
	bool "Build bounded op6893 SCP mailbox receive transactions"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_PROTOCOL
	help
	  Build an ordered copy/ack/deliver backend over caller-supplied
	  operations, with sticky failures and exact READY0/READY1 validation.
	  A future provider must own clocks, IRQ containment and reset generation.
	  This registers no device or IRQ, performs no automatic hardware access
	  and cannot start SCP/MD or establish READY by itself.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_PENDING_OBSERVE
	bool "Allow explicit op6893 mailbox pending observation"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_OBSERVE=y && OF_IRQ
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_CORE0_OBSERVE && OP6893_CCCI_SCP_PROTOCOL
	help
	  Map only five mailbox CLR/pending words and parse IRQ specifiers
	  without mapping or requesting Linux IRQs. Explicitly sample pending
	  twice under before/after core0/mux checks and compare with the full
	  mailbox layout. No ACK, payload reads, IRQ enable or READY acceptance.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_DRAIN
	bool "Build op6893 SCP bounded receive drain and lifetime backend"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_RX
	help
	  Build a process-context backend that masks all mailbox sources, drains
	  complete bounded sweeps and rejects stale queued generations. Failures
	  invalidate all RX instances and retain masking. STOP is split around
	  the caller's IRQ/worker synchronization. This has no device, IRQ or
	  workqueue caller and does not perform reset or establish SCP READY.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_QUEUE
	bool "Build op6893 SCP bounded CPU receive queue adapter"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_RX
	help
	  Reserve complete-batch CPU queue capacity before the board completion
	  and mailbox acknowledgment. Copy every RX pin into generation-tagged
	  CPU storage after ACK. Queue exhaustion faults without consuming that
	  batch. No device, IRQ, worker, MMIO caller or READY handler is added.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_IRQ_RESERVE
	bool "Reserve op6893 mailbox IRQs without enabling receive"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_CFG_RESERVE && OF_IRQ
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_QUEUE
	help
	  Request five dedicated level-high mailbox IRQs with NO_AUTOEN in the
	  existing cfg/resource owner. All remain disabled; no arm operation is
	  provided. Unexpected handlers only contain and schedule fault cleanup.
	  Teardown closes scheduling before IRQ/worker synchronization outside
	  the owner mutex. No mailbox MMIO, completion, reset or READY is added.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_MMIO
	bool "Build op6893 non-posted SCP mailbox RX register backend"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_RX && HAS_IOMEM && ARM64_4K_PAGES
	help
	  Build a helper that reserves complete cfg/mailbox pages with non-posted
	  mappings and supplies ordered RX copy/completion/ACK operations. A future
	  unique owner must replace its old cfg/pending mappings, establish real
	  reset generations and serialize prerequisites, IRQ/work and clients.
	  Enabling it alone registers no device and performs no hardware access.
	  The separate MMIO_RESERVE opt-in only connects resource mapping in the
	  unique owner. The receive queue supplies destinations for its hardware
	  ops; no RX caller, reset operation or READY acceptance is added.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_MMIO_RESERVE
	bool "Reserve non-posted SCP cfg/mailbox pages in the unique owner"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_MMIO && OP6893_CCCI_SCP_IRQ_RESERVE
	depends on !OP6893_CCCI_SCP_PENDING_OBSERVE
	help
	  Replace the old cfg mapping with six complete non-posted pages in the
	  existing resource owner. Reject resource conflicts and mapping errors.
	  Exclude the old pending observer to avoid overlapping mappings with
	  different attributes. Probe does not access registers or prepare RX;
	  all five NO_AUTOEN IRQs remain masked. Sysfs only reports bookkeeping.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_RECEIVE
	bool "Build the op6893 SCP IRQ/work receive adapter"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_MMIO_RESERVE && OP6893_CCCI_SCP_DRAIN
	help
	  Build the Linux IRQ/work adapter for non-posted MMIO, all RX queues and
	  bounded drains. It balances one IRQ disable depth, captures generation
	  at queue time and closes scheduling before STOP synchronization. A future
	  owner must establish real reset generations before starting receive.
	  The separate RECEIVE_RESERVE opt-in connects only the dormant constructor
	  in place of the legacy IRQ reservation. No start/arm, reset or READY
	  interface is provided.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_RECEIVE_RESERVE
	bool "Reserve the dormant op6893 SCP receive adapter in the unique owner"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_RECEIVE
	help
	  Replace the legacy IRQ reservation with the receive adapter in the
	  existing resource owner. Request five NO_AUTOEN IRQs without preparing
	  RX, reading or writing registers, or calling the resource check. The
	  prerequisite wrapper rejects every generation until a future reset
	  owner establishes real old-message isolation. No start/arm interface,
	  reset write, IRQ enable or READY acceptance is provided.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_CORE_TCM_RESERVE
	bool "Reserve op6893 SCP core0/core1/TCM in the unique owner"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_RECEIVE_RESERVE
	depends on !OP6893_CCCI_SCP_CORE0_OBSERVE
	help
	  Reserve the complete same-board core0/core1 configuration pages and
	  TCM with non-posted mappings in the boot-lifetime resource owner.
	  Exclude the legacy core0 observer and its dependent TCM/pending readers
	  to prevent overlapping aliases. Geometry and exclusive claims are
	  checked before publishing the set. No register or TCM I/O, reset,
	  restore, IRQ enable or SCP/MD start operation is provided. The AP-side
	  clock/reservation observer may remain enabled without its SCP readers.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_OWNER_OBSERVE
	bool "Allow explicit core/header observations in the unique SCP owner"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_CORE_TCM_RESERVE
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_RESTORE_PLAN && OF_RESERVED_MEM && MFD_SYSCON
	help
	  Observe both cores' reset aliases and gated/halt bits, and an exact
	  68/72-byte TCM header through the existing unique mappings. Explicit
	  sysfs reads require a valid 26 MHz pin and before/after clock and mux
	  checks under the owner mutex. Report only bounded metadata and CPU
	  recovery geometry. No register/TCM read or resource query is made at
	  probe. No reset, copying, IRQ enable, start or READY claim is added.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_RESET_ASSERT
	bool "Allow one explicit vendor-style op6893 SCP dual-core reset assertion"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_OWNER_OBSERVE
	help
	  Stop and synchronize the receive adapter, then perform the same-board
	  non-secure vendor forced-reset sequence: SET bit0 on both cores and
	  DSB SY, followed by SET readbacks. Requires the explicit 26 MHz pin
	  and valid TOPCK. One request per boot; no CLR, restore, pending ACK,
	  IRQ enable or SCP/MD start. SET readback does not prove all DMA or
	  old messages isolated. Disabled by default, no operation at probe.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_INITIAL_BOOT
	bool "Allow one bounded op6893 SCP initial boot and READY test"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_RESET_ASSERT
	help
	  Explicit initial_boot sysfs test: stop RX, assert both cores, validate
	  LK header geometry, discard known old notifications, prepare all RX
	  destinations and release core0 with this boot's share reservation.
	  Accept READY0 or READY1 only through the generation-tagged IRQ/queue.
	  On success or after three seconds, stop RX and assert both cores again.
	  Other client messages are consumed without following firmware pointers.
	  One attempt per boot, disabled by default, no automatic start at probe.
	  This does not restore firmware, keep SCP running or start the modem.

config OP6893_CCCI_SCP_RUNTIME
	bool "Allow explicit op6893 SCP runtime, AP awake and MD-invalid notification"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SCP_INITIAL_BOOT && OP6893_CCCI_SCP_AWAKE
	select CRC32
	help
	  Start one SCP generation with an IRQ-worker CPU event consumer, accept
	  READY0/1 and test a paired AP awake lock/unlock. Keep SCP running until
	  explicit stop or a contained receive/awake/protocol fault. Consume logger
	  notifications without following firmware pointers. Optionally send one
	  APCCCI MD-invalid notification; no shared-memory init or modem startup.
	  Disabled by default. No start, handshake or notification occurs at probe.

config OP6893_CCCI_CCISM
	bool "Build the op6893 post-HS2 CCISM exchange"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_HANDSHAKE && OP6893_CCCI_SCP_RUNTIME
	help
	  Bounded CCISM INIT/ACK/RBREADY/DONE state machine using the same-board
	  6.6 sequence, with explicit SCP generation, deadlines and stopped-MD
	  shutdown. A unique bridge reserves CCIF2 and exact ID16 pages, holds
	  inherited clock aliases, invokes SMC13 and uses ordinary system-port
	  TX and a leased SCP client. A bounded worker handles replies and timers.
	  No platform start caller, MD CPU release or automatic action is added.
	  Disabled by default; completion is distinct from radio readiness.

config OP6893_CCCI_SERVICES
	bool "Build experimental op6893 FS/RPC services and backend endpoint"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_HANDSHAKE
	help
	  Add exact FS fragment reassembly, RPC framing and ownership, and a
	  bounded generation/request-token router over explicit backend callbacks.
	  Include ordinary FS/RPC TX with transport-owned sequence and assert.
	  Add an ordered worker and exclusive privileged experimental backend
	  endpoint. No filesystem mount, hardware RPC provider or service-ready
	  gate is installed. No CPU release or automatic start.
	  Disabled by default; prototype user tools operate only on caller-supplied
	  private working copies and do not establish bootstrap service readiness.

config OP6893_CCCI_DISPATCH
	bool "Build op6893 accepted-handshake and normal-port dispatcher"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_SERVICES && OP6893_CCCI_CCISM
	help
	  Route accepted post-publication HS1 to service start, accepted HS2 to
	  service sequence state and post-HS2 CCISM, and normal FS/RPC/system
	  packets to their unique owners. Reserve the exact backend and SCP lease
	  before a future MD release, with sticky deferred fault containment and
	  stopped-MD cleanup. No automatic prepare/start, CPU release, populated
	  RPC facts, NVRAM cache population or service-ready gate is provided.
	  Disabled by default. Construction performs no hardware or protocol I/O.

config OP6893_CCCI_NVRAM_CACHE
	bool "Build the op6893 feature-36 NVRAM cache owner"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_MD_PLATFORM && OP6893_CCCI_SMEM
	help
	  Take the single AP ownership of the cached SMEM user-32 window that
	  feature 36 advertises. Prepare maps it write-combined and applies the
	  same-board first-start clear once; later reconnects and stops never
	  re-zero a live cache. No cache image is loaded, no header is invented
	  and no region content is exported. Construction performs no I/O.
	  Disabled by default.


config OP6893_CCCI_MD_BOOT
	bool "Build the gated op6893 MD CPU release owner"
	depends on OP6893_CCCI_DISPATCH && OP6893_CCCI_NVRAM_CACHE && NVMEM
	help
	  Add the unique MD boot owner. Prepare is the ready gate: prepare the
	  ordinary CCIF rings, map and first-clear the feature-36 cache, build
	  typed runtime offers from the validated LK layout and reserve the
	  connected FS backend plus real SCP lease. Release starts RX/handshake
	  and then issues the same-board (6,0) MD CPU boot SMC exactly once.
	  A service stop requires parent MD1 domain OFF readback as hardware
	  evidence; RX closure, faults or generation changes are not evidence.
	  No automatic action or sysfs trigger runs at probe. Disabled by default.

config OP6893_CCCI_DPMAIF
	bool "op6893 DPMAIF diagnostics and raw IP interface"
	depends on ARCH_MEDIATEK && OF && HAS_IOMEM && COMMON_CLK_MT6893_PMIF && NET
	help
	  Map the DPMAIF registers and register a raw IP interface for the
	  first modem data channel. Probe leaves the hardware untouched.
	  The operator must arm both rings before bringing the interface up.
